Data Center Registry

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs

Data Center Registry is an open-source, vendor-neutral canonical registry for
data-center identities, site membership, control-plane generations, lifecycle
state and authoritative facility metadata. It is the first repository of the
Data Center Control Plane (DCCP) Tranche 1 and owns the authoritative physical
identity model that higher control layers compose.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Data Center Registry does not collect or transmit any telemetry. All state,
logs and evidence are written to local files chosen by the operator and never
leave the machine running the software.

Data Center Registry accepts contributions from individuals and organizations
on the terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a Contributor License
Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution guidance.
